                        "sense_id": "300f2d52-c490-3cbd-a61b-421a9a75a214",
                        "entry_id": "39531989-5426-3adc-b39a-c0870409e5c7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A Mexican American, especially a juvenile delinquent in the Los Angeles area."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b50dc194-acbd-40bb-a8e3-057ab1debc41",
                                "sense_id": "300f2d52-c490-3cbd-a61b-421a9a75a214",
                                "text": "Now they saw that Terry was Mexican, a Pachuco wildcat; and that her boy was worse than that."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "117566ab-947d-4547-a785-7eb5ecc1ff25",
                                "sense_id": "300f2d52-c490-3cbd-a61b-421a9a75a214",
                                "text": "I moved farther and farther into the Chicano community. I took Spanish in school and found willing tutors among my friends, who taught me a real-life version of the standard textbook language. I began to dress and comb my hair in the pachuco style of the day. I acquired the social customs and mannerisms of those around me."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ffcb6a5b-e564-4f7a-b415-41159c0fdc4f",
                                "sense_id": "300f2d52-c490-3cbd-a61b-421a9a75a214",
                                "text": "They asked him if he was a pachuco. He said all the pachucos he knew of lived in El Paso. He told em he didn’t know any Mexican pachucos."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ea4cb132-56c3-367c-8206-94a8e7249288",
                        "entry_id": "39531989-5426-3adc-b39a-c0870409e5c7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An argot spoken by that group, sometimes known as caló."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "18ecad63-00d6-42f8-810d-20c9f11afc0f",
                                "sense_id": "ea4cb132-56c3-367c-8206-94a8e7249288",
                                "text": "Like the zoot suit, the Pachuco caló was adopted by a large part of the Chicano youth who did not, in essence, identify themselves as Pachucos."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
